  "caption": "Quinn signed up for a fun run and went from zero to running every day. By day five, the shins were not having it.\n\nShin splints usually show up when impact jumps faster than bone and tissues can adapt: more kilometres, harder surfaces, or coming back at your old pace. Training load often matters more than foot shape.\n\nWhat can help: turn the running down rather than off, keep fit with cycling, swimming or pool running, build calf strength step by step, and return with run-walk intervals, adding about 10% a week.\n\nSharp pinpoint pain on the bone, pain at rest or at night, or pain that worsens each run is worth getting checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
